<section class="eg-section eg-paper" id="buyer-routes"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Start with what the product changes</p><h2>Two fintech offers. Different buyers.</h2><p>A payments platform selling to merchants needs a different campaign from a verification provider selling to lenders. Choose the route closest to your offer.</p></div><div class="eg-grid eg-paths">
<details open><summary>Payments technology → merchants</summary><p><strong>Target:</strong> ecommerce and multi-location merchants with payment operations your platform can support.</p><p><strong>Reach:</strong> finance, payments, ecommerce and operations owners. Confirm who manages the current provider and who would evaluate a change.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> “Where does the current payment setup still create work for your team?”</p><div class="eg-record"><p class="eg-kicker">Illustrative meeting note</p><dl><div><dt>Buyer-confirmed question</dt><dd>How can finance reconcile online and in-store payments with less manual work?</dd></div><div><dt>Agreed next step</dt><dd>A focused discussion with the finance owner about that workflow.</dd></div><div><dt>Still to establish</dt><dd>Platform compatibility, project timing and the commercial case.</dd></div></dl><p class="eg-small">Fictional example of a handoff. No actual prospect or booked meeting is represented.</p></div><a class="eg-link" href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/payment-processing-cold-call-script/">Use the payment processing script →</a></details>
<details><summary>Lending technology → institutions</summary><p><strong>Target:</strong> credit unions and lenders whose lending process fits your product and supported markets.</p><p><strong>Reach:</strong> lending, underwriting and operations owners, with technology and control specialists brought in when needed.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> “Which income-evidence steps still need someone to review exceptions manually?”</p><div class="eg-record"><p class="eg-kicker">Illustrative meeting note</p><dl><div><dt>Buyer-confirmed question</dt><dd>How does the current verification process handle incomplete applicant evidence?</dd></div><div><dt>Agreed next step</dt><dd>A workflow review with the lending operations owner.</dd></div><div><dt>Still to establish</dt><dd>Data availability, integration requirements and the evaluation process.</dd></div></dl><p class="eg-small">Fictional example of a handoff. Product capabilities must be confirmed by your specialists.</p></div><a class="eg-link" href="/articles/sell-income-verification-software-lending-leaders/">Read the income-verification sales guide →</a></details></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section" id="delivery"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">A managed front end to your sales process</p><h2>Agree the work. Keep the ownership clear.</h2></div><div class="eg-grid"><article class="eg-card"><h3>CallTeam runs the agreed outreach.</h3><ul><li>Define suitable accounts, buyer roles and exclusions.</li><li>Prepare contacts and a credible reason for the call.</li><li>Make human calls and handle agreed follow-up.</li><li>Qualify the response, schedule the next conversation and prepare the handoff.</li><li>Review results and use buyer feedback to improve the campaign.</li></ul></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Your specialists move the evaluation.</h3><ul><li>Approve product claims, targeting and relevant evidence.</li><li>Answer technical, security and implementation questions.</li><li>Provide meeting availability and act on useful introductions.</li><li>Run demonstrations, evaluate the opportunity and manage proposals and closing.</li></ul></article></div><div class="eg-download"><div><strong>Use the fintech meeting-handoff checklist.</strong><p>Editable plain text: account fit, buyer, workflow, agreement and open questions.</p></div><a class="eg-button eg-secondary" href="/assets/downloads/CallTeam-Fintech-Meeting-Handoff-Checklist.txt" download>Download the Checklist ↓</a></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section eg-paper" id="evidence"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Published CallTeam campaign evidence</p><h2>See what happened in two past engagements.</h2><p>Read the target market, qualification and execution behind each result. The figures describe the stated campaign and period.</p></div><div class="eg-grid"><article class="eg-card"><p class="eg-kicker">Payment platform / 90 days</p><span class="eg-stat">15 demos</span><h3>Three closed deals.</h3><p>The campaign focused on ecommerce and multi-location merchants with payment complexity and a useful reason to review their environment.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/case-studies/fintech-payment-platform-appointment-setting/">Read the payments case study →</a></article><article class="eg-card"><p class="eg-kicker">Income verification / 90 days</p><span class="eg-stat">8 meetings</span><h3>Two new customers.</h3><p>The lending technology campaign reached credit unions around income-evidence workflows. Two further opportunities were advancing in the reported period.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/case-studies/credit-union-income-verification-appointment-setting/">Read the lending technology case study →</a></article></div><p class="eg-small">Confidential client engagements published by CallTeam. Outcomes depend on the offer, market, scope and sales follow-through.</p></div></section>
<section class="eg-section" id="investment"><div class="eg-wrap eg-split"><div><p class="eg-kicker">Scope and investment</p><h2>Build the economics around your sale.</h2><p>Agree the market, research, calling coverage, follow-up and meeting standard before setting the scope. Check current pricing and identify the decisions your team needs to make before launch.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/pricing/">See CallTeam pricing →</a></div><div class="eg-card"><h3>Test the business case with your assumptions.</h3><p>Use customer value, margin, campaign cost and closing assumptions to explore return and break-even. A calculation is useful when its inputs fit your business.</p><a class="eg-button" href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Calculate Your Campaign ROI →</a></div></div></section>
